  "summary": "Recent C. elegans work links lifespan to stress pathways, NAD+ remodeling, UPRmt signaling and midlife architectural change, with temperature and context effects.",
  "synthesis": "The items share C. elegans aging as a system in which lifespan extension depends on context. Dietary HSP90 acts through DAF-16, SKN-1 and HSF-1. Methionine restriction requires intestinal UPRmt activation, PKC-1 and the neuropeptides INS-27, INS-34 and INS-35. Developmental daf-2 knockdown extends lifespan at 15°C but not 25°C, with a temperature-dependent skn-1 requirement. Rapamycin delays amyloid-β proteotoxicity without reducing amyloid burden. Systems-level work adds two findings: NAD+ rises with age despite remodeled biosynthesis and salvage, and the MoMA strain reveals an abrupt midlife shift in subcellular architecture. Together these emphasize conditional, multi-branch regulation and organism-level readouts of aging, though the items test different interventions and are not a single mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
